14 files are untouched. `LICENSE` is upstream's, copied and not counted.

Not upstream, written by PIE, and NO LONGER IN THIS DIRECTORY:

    bit                          std::bit_cast, for fp16.h
    boost/math/ccmath/fabs.hpp   one constexpr fabs, for fp16.h
    cstdint                      the eight fixed-width typedefs
    cuda.h                       CUDA_VERSION, derived from __CUDACC_VER_*
    cuda_runtime.h               ushort/uchar, and <cstdint>
    type_traits                  integral_constant and six things built on it

These six sat here for a provenance reason -- they exist BECAUSE FlashInfer
asks for them, so they were filed under FlashInfer.  That is the wrong axis.
What they DO is impersonate a header this compiler does not ship, which is
also what `cuda_fp16.h`, `cuda_bf16.h`, `cuda_fp8.h`, `cuda_fp4.h`,
`cooperative_groups.h` and `cuda/{cmath,pipeline,std/limits}` do, and those
eight sat under `csrc/src/` for the mirror-image reason: our own text asks for
them too.  All fourteen are now in `csrc/shim/`, filed by role.

The move cannot be seen from inside a compile.  NVRTC has no `-I`: it matches
the literal string in the directive against the names in `includeNames[]`, and
those names are unchanged, because for a shim THE NAME IS THE CONTRACT -- a
file called `cuda_fp16.h` is answering for NVIDIA's `cuda_fp16.h` and cannot
be renamed without ceasing to do its job.  nvcc needed one line: a second
`-iquote` at each of the four sites that pass the first.

Nothing in this table moved, and nothing in it changed.  The transform above
still recovers upstream v0.6.15 byte for byte from every file listed, which is
the point of doing the shim group first -- it is the one role whose files are
neither vendored nor included by relative path from a vendored file, so it
moves without editing a single upstream byte.
